      "title": "DNA only gets built ONE way. Why?",
      "narration": "DNA only gets built one way. Here's why. Every strand has two different ends. The 5-prime end. And the 3-prime end. New pieces can only snap onto the 3-prime end. One way. Every time. New DNA only grows from 5-prime to 3-prime. But it can't start from nothing. Swipe.",
